This is the first post on the new site. The plan is simple: write more, write longer, and trust the index to find anything worth keeping.

## Why a new blog

I had a portfolio. It worked, but it didn't invite writing. The friction was real — every "I should publish this" became "I'll add it to drafts" became nothing.

So I rebuilt around writing. The stack is small enough that pushing a new post is a two-minute exercise, and good enough that I won't have to migrate again next year.

{% callout type="tip" %}
The whole thing is **Astro on Cloudflare Workers**. Content is markdown in git, edited via [Keystatic](https://keystatic.com). Drafts live on PR preview URLs until I merge.
{% /callout %}

## What you'll find here

Three threads, roughly:

1. **Engineering** — what I'm building, what broke, what I'd do differently.
1. **Photography** — equipment, processing, the occasional gallery.
1. **Craft** — slower notes on tools, workflows, and the boring parts that make work feel good.

There's an English and a Ukrainian version of the site. They're not auto-translated — each language is hand-written, and I'll only publish in the language I can do justice to.

```ts
// A tiny taste of the code that runs this
import { getPublishedPosts } from '../lib/posts';

const posts = await getPublishedPosts('en');
for (const post of posts) {
  console.log(post.data.title);
}
```

## Subscribing

If you want to follow along, hit the **Subscribe** link in the header. It's a personal cadence — no calendar, no newsletter platform. Just emails when there's something worth sending.

Thanks for reading.
